# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HeartGuard (PV-MEPCG / PulseVision) — .gitignore
# Written in Phase 01, BEFORE the first `git add`. Two entries below are the
# reason this file exists at all: dataset/ is 1.3 GB of read-only input and
# must never be staged, and cache/ holds regenerable preprocessed signals and
# feature shards.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw datasets — read-only input, 1.3 GB, never committed
dataset/

# Derived / regenerable artifacts (directory kept, contents ignored)
cache/*
!cache/.gitkeep

# Feature matrices and other columnar dumps
*.parquet

# Experiment resume state (Phase 63). One JSON + one parquet per (model, fold),
# ~4 MB for a 25-fold six-model run and pure working state: every number in it
# is already in the committed per_fold_metrics.csv and aggregate_metrics.csv.
# It exists so an interrupted run resumes, not as a deliverable.
outputs/**/_checkpoints/

# Run logs — rotating, machine-local, regenerated on every run. The directory
# itself is kept (outputs/logs/.gitkeep). run_manifest.json and
# evidence_index.csv are NOT ignored: both are named deliverables (T102.5).
outputs/logs/*.log
outputs/logs/*.log.*
outputs/logs/htmlcov/
report.log

# Coverage
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Trained model binaries (the directory itself is kept).
# Recursive: Phase 51 writes models_saved/{task}/{model_id}/model.joblib, which
# the single-level pattern below it does NOT match — M4 alone is 12 MB and M6
# is 15 MB. The manifests beside them are small JSON and ARE committed: they
# carry the size, fit time, inference time and feature-name list, which are the
# actual deliverables. The binaries are reproducible from a seeded run.
models_saved/**/*.pkl
models_saved/**/*.joblib

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Virtual environment
.venv/

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
# NOTE: frontend/out/ is deliberately NOT ignored — the exported static
# dashboard is committed so a grader without Node can serve it from FastAPI.

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
junit.xml

# Planning and working documents — kept local by the user's decision
# (2026-08-23). todo.md, note.md and the two source documents are NOT pushed.
# NOTE: they remain in commits f440a24..b817e84 on the remote; this rule stops
# future pushes only. CLAUDE.md at the repo root stays tracked.
Docs/

# Search results produced under an objective that was subsequently changed
# (2026-08-28). Kept on disk as the evidence behind that decision -- see the
# README.txt inside and the 2026-08-28 entry in Docs/note.md -- but never
# committed: no number in them matches configs/experiments.yaml as it stands.
outputs/05_search_optimization/_superseded_*/
